================================================================================

=== REASONING ===

Eight rubber-duck adjustments adopted before any code was written:

1. Don't auto-index docs at boot. F7 ships the library + retriever
   factory + TTL cron only. N6 (the RAG-backed help chatbot) will
   own its own indexer scheduling behind its own AI feature gate.
   This preserves §I1 (default-off) and §I4 (zero default egress)
   for the docs corpus.

2. PgvectorRetriever takes a ProviderResolver, NOT a raw Provider.
   Every Embed call therefore flows through F1's audit-decorated
   Registry → F3's ai_call_log writes. Cannot be bypassed.

3. Wrap ctx with audit.WithSubject + audit.WithFeatureID before
   every Embed call. The audit decorator uses ctx values for
   user_subject + feature_id columns; missing them = un-attributable
   row.

4. Index workflow is incremental:
     a. SELECT existing (chunk_idx, text_hash) for this source row.
     b. Compute new hashes; embed only changed chunks.
     c. UPSERT changed; DELETE chunks where chunk_idx >= len(new).
   This makes re-indexing idempotent and keeps the Embed budget
   minimal (matches §I7 — per-feature rate limits stay meaningful).

5. expires_at uses a year-9999 sentinel for never-expire (docs)
   instead of `'infinity'::timestamptz`. Reason: pgx's default scan
   type for `infinity` triggers a round-trip mode switch on the
   timestamptz codec which complicates downstream model marshalling.
   Year 9999 sorts identically and round-trips as a normal time.

6. Vector extension version assertion parses extversion as []int
   (semver-safe) instead of TEXT lexicographic compare. Migration
   000205 fails fast if vector < 0.5.0 (HNSW requirement).

7. Score column = cosine SIMILARITY in [-1, 1], NOT [0, 1]. The SQL
   selects `1 - (embedding <=> $1::vector)` so consumers can rank
   directly. Document this on the Chunk struct comment.

8. Defensive limits: cap k at 100; reject NaN/Inf vector elements at
   the Index boundary; validate dim matches table's VECTOR(n) before
   INSERT. Surfaced as ErrInvalidVector / ErrChunkLimitExceeded.

ADR-015 invariants preserved:

  §I1 default-off:        rag.New() returns NoopRetriever when
                          settings.AIMode() == "off". A no-op cannot
                          embed, write rows, or dial out.
  §I4 zero default egress: NoopRetriever's Index/Retrieve/Forget all
                          return (zero-value, nil) without touching
                          the provider, the database, or the network.
  §I7 single canonical surface: rag.Retriever is the ONLY way a
                          feature can do similarity search. There is
                          no second SQL helper, no second pgvector
                          import, no second Embed dispatch path.
  §I8 graceful degradation: factory.New() fails closed — any error
                          loading settings (DB down, malformed JSON)
                          returns a NoopRetriever, never panics or
                          returns a half-initialised real retriever.
  §I12 runtime mode flips: jobs.RunEmbeddingsTTL re-reads AIMode at
                          tick time. If an operator flips off mid-
                          run, the next tick exits early without
                          opening a transaction.

P7 (single Retrieve entry) honoured: every consumer (N3, N6, D2,
D5, C4 in later slices) goes through rag.Retriever.Retrieve. No
direct `embedding <=> $` SQL is allowed outside internal/ai/rag/.

