=== CHANGES ===

A. Migrations (vector ext + symmetric embeddings tables):

  migrations/000205_enable_vector.up.sql   (new)
    CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector + DO-block version
    assertion. Parses extversion via string_to_array → INT[] for
    safe semver compare; fails the migration if vector < 0.5.0
    (HNSW requirement).

  migrations/000205_enable_vector.down.sql (new)
    Intentional no-op (DROP EXTENSION would cascade to embeddings_*
    tables and is rolled back by 000206/d anyway). Documented
    inline.

  migrations/000206_embeddings.up.sql      (new)
    Two physical tables — embeddings_768 (nomic-embed-text default,
    Ollama-friendly) + embeddings_1536 (text-embedding-3-small,
    OpenAI-friendly). Each has:
      - user_subject TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '' (single-tenant
        adaptation, see SURVEY §3)
      - source_type, source_id, chunk_idx, text, text_hash, model,
        created_at, expires_at
      - UNIQUE (user_subject, source_type, source_id, chunk_idx,
        model) for hash-deduped upserts
      - HNSW index on (embedding vector_cosine_ops) WITH
        (m=16, ef_construction=64)
      - btree on (user_subject, source_type) for source_type
        filters
      - btree on (expires_at) for the TTL cron's range scan
      - CHECK constraints: source_id non-empty, hash non-empty,
        model non-empty, chunk_idx >= 0

  migrations/000206_embeddings.down.sql    (new)
    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS embeddings_768 CASCADE + same for
    embeddings_1536. Note: does NOT drop the dormant phase-39
    `embeddings` table (vector(384), unrelated, never owned by F7).

B. internal/ai/rag/ (new package, Layer: platform):

  doc.go                     Package doc + Layer header.
  rag.go                     Public surface:
                               - type Chunk { SourceType, SourceID,
                                 ChunkIdx, Text, Score float32 }
                               - type Retriever interface { Retrieve,
                                 Index, Forget }
                               - constants: TableEmbeddings768,
                                 TableEmbeddings1536, ModelNomic,
                                 ModelOpenAISmall, MaxK=100
                               - TTLPolicy map[string]time.Duration
                               - Source* string consts (drive_summary,
                                 charge_session, alert_history,
                                 automation_run, docs, user_note)
  noop.go                    NoopRetriever — Index/Retrieve/Forget
                             return (zero, nil) with zero side
                             effects. Type-system proof of §I4 for
                             off-mode.
  vector.go                  Pure-Go helpers: encodeVector(serialise
                             []float32 → pgvector text format
                             "[v1,v2,...]"); decodeVector (parse
                             back); validateVector (reject NaN/Inf,
                             enforce dim).
  chunker.go                 ChunkText(text, maxRunes, overlap) →
                             []string. Word-boundary preserving,
                             rune-count safe (multi-byte aware),
                             never returns empty chunks. Function
                             name is ChunkText not Chunk because
                             type Chunk already exists.
  ttl.go                     SourceTTL(sourceType) → time.Duration;
                             ExpiresAt(now, sourceType) → time.Time
                             with year-9999 sentinel for never-expire
                             sources.
  pgvector.go                PgvectorRetriever — the production
                             implementation. Holds:
                               - *pgxpool.Pool
                               - ProviderResolver (so Embed runs
                                 through audit decorator)
                               - model string + tableName + dim
                             Methods:
                               - Retrieve: WithSubject + WithFeatureID
                                 → resolver.ResolveForFeature →
                                 prov.Embed(query) → SELECT … ORDER BY
                                 embedding <=> $vec LIMIT k. Returns
                                 cosine similarity 1 - distance.
                               - Index: SELECT existing (chunk_idx,
                                 text_hash) → diff → embed only
                                 changed → tx { UPSERT changed,
                                 DELETE stale chunk_idx } → commit.
                                 All Embed calls go through the
                                 resolver.
                               - Forget: DELETE WHERE
                                 (user_subject, source_type,
                                 source_id) — used by user-data
                                 deletion flow + N6 corrections.
                             ProviderResolver interface narrowed to
                             { ResolveForFeature(ctx, featureID)
                             (Provider, error) } — *provider.Registry
                             satisfies it directly.
  factory.go                 New(ctx, deps) Retriever:
                               1. Read settings.AIMode().
                               2. mode == "off" → return Noop.
                               3. mode != "off" → construct
                                  PgvectorRetriever with the
                                  configured embedding model.
                               4. Settings load error → log + Noop
                                  (fail closed, §I8).
  docs_indexer.go            DocsIndexer.IndexAll(ctx, retriever) —
                             walks docs/user/**/*.md, splits by H2
                             headings, calls retriever.Index per
                             section. NOT scheduled by F7; the
                             package-level call site lives behind
                             the N6 feature gate (per rubber-duck
                             adjustment #1).
  noop_test.go               Asserts every NoopRetriever method
                             returns (zero, nil) and emits zero
                             counters. §I4 evidence at type level.
  vector_test.go             encode/decode round-trip + reject
                             NaN/Inf + dim mismatch.
  chunker_test.go            Word-boundary + rune-safe + overlap
                             coverage.
  ttl_test.go                Per-source-type policy + year-9999
                             sentinel.
  factory_test.go            Spy ProviderResolver: asserts ZERO
                             Embed calls when ai_mode=off (proves
                             §I4 dynamically as well as statically).
  docs_indexer_test.go       Walk + split goldens (in-memory FS).
  pgvector_test.go           DSN-gated live test against the local
                             timescaledb-ha:pg17 + vector 0.8.2.
                             Covers: Index round-trip, Retrieve
                             top-k ordering, Forget, dim-mismatch
