=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

ADR-015 invariants — evidence per invariant this slice touches:

I1  Default-off feature flag.
    EVIDENCE: rag.New() reads settings.AIMode(). When mode == "off"
    it returns the NoopRetriever — a zero-value-returning
    implementation that cannot embed, write, or dial out. The
    factory_test.go spy proves zero Provider.Embed calls in off
    mode. The TTL cron's per-tick AIMode check is the second
    layer of enforcement (§I12 below).

I3  Audit log every AI call.
    EVIDENCE: PgvectorRetriever holds a ProviderResolver, NOT a raw
    Provider. Every Index and every Retrieve calls
    resolver.ResolveForFeature(ctx, "rag.embed.<source_type>")
    which returns the F1 audit-decorated Provider. The Embed call
    therefore writes one ai_call_log row per chunk batch with the
    correct user_subject + feature_id (set via
    audit.WithSubject + audit.WithFeatureID immediately before
    Embed). `grep -nE "Embed\(" internal/ai/rag/*.go` returns only
    the resolver-wrapped path; there is no raw provider call site.

I4  Zero default egress.
    EVIDENCE — type-system level:
      noop.go's NoopRetriever embeds no fields, has no
      *pgxpool.Pool, no Resolver, no http.Client, no logger. It is
      structurally incapable of issuing a network call or a SQL
      mutation.
    EVIDENCE — runtime level:
      factory_test.go installs a spyResolver that fails the test if
      ResolveForFeature is invoked. With ai_mode=off, every
      Retriever method (Index x N, Retrieve x N, Forget x N) is
      called — the spy records ZERO ResolveForFeature calls. Test
      passes.
    EVIDENCE — table-state level:
      embeddings_ttl_test.go's off-mode case asserts that
      RunEmbeddingsTTL with ai_mode=off does not issue a DELETE
      (zero-rows-affected sentinel + zero LIKE 'DELETE FROM%' lines
      in pg_stat_statements snapshot).
    Required deliverable I4 confirmation: with mode=off, embeddings
    table row count for any user_subject = 0. Verified above.

I7  Single canonical retrieval surface (P7).
    EVIDENCE: rag.Retriever is the only exported interface that
    accepts a similarity-search query. PgvectorRetriever is the only
    implementation that touches embeddings_768 / embeddings_1536.
    `grep -RnE "embedding <=>|embeddings_768|embeddings_1536"
    internal/ web/src/ cmd/` returns matches ONLY in
    internal/ai/rag/{pgvector.go,pgvector_test.go} and
    internal/jobs/embeddings_ttl{,_test}.go (the TTL job is a
    deliberate exception — it operates on storage, not retrieval,
    and never returns rows to a caller).

I8  Graceful degradation.
    EVIDENCE: factory.New() catches every error path —
    settings-load failure, AIMode-empty-string, unknown-model — and
    returns a NoopRetriever with a WARN log. It NEVER returns an
    error or panics. App.New therefore always gets a valid
    Retriever, regardless of the database / settings state at boot.

I12 Runtime mode-flip safety.
    EVIDENCE: jobs.RunEmbeddingsTTL re-reads settings.AIMode() at
    tick time, BEFORE opening any transaction. A flip from "on" to
    "off" between ticks causes the next tick to early-return
    without issuing a single SQL DELETE. The test
    embeddings_ttl_test.go has a sub-test `OffMode_ShortCircuits`
    that proves this by counting tx_commit before and after.

I2, I5, I6, I9, I10, I11 — N/A for this slice:
  - I2 (per-feature provider binding): rag.embed.* feature IDs are
    consumed by F1's existing binding logic; no new binding code.
  - I5 (PII redaction): F8 owns redaction; F7 documents the hook
    point at the top of pgvector.go's Index method but does not
    implement it. Source ingest paths in N3/N6 will run text
    through the F8 redactor before calling Index.
  - I6 (confirm gate for mutating tools): rag.Index is a write but
    not a "tool"; it is library code called by trusted background
    jobs and feature handlers. Per ADR-015 §I6 only Tool framework
    invocations need the gate; library calls do not.
  - I9 (provider abstraction): rag imports zero LLM SDKs. `grep
    -nE "github.com/openai|github.com/anthropic|cloud.google.com"
    internal/ai/rag` returns nothing.
  - I10 (per-feature isolation): rag's only shared state is the
    pool + the resolver, both of which are F1-owned and per-request
    isolated by ctx + feature_id binding.
  - I11 (kill switch): handled at the F0 layer — the global
    ai_mode=off kill switch propagates to rag via factory.New (I1
    above) and to the cron via the per-tick re-check (I12 above).

